// R5 lane PAR-MARGIN M10 (the frozen shape): a default-percent (390 %) buy stop placed ABOVE the
// session's last close (2025-4-23 15:45 America/New_York), not marketable when placed, gapped
// through by the next session's open. Margin 25: the entry bar's low breaches. Which book does
// TradingView size the entry, and its entry-bar margin call, on -- the signal-time units or the
// units the fill opens? Timeout close 3 bars after the entry bar.
//@version=6
strategy("pm-m10-f-gapup-0424", overlay=true, initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=390, pyramiding=1,
     margin_long=25, margin_short=25, commission_value=0, slippage=0,
     process_orders_on_close=false)
if time == timestamp("America/New_York", 2025, 4, 23, 15, 45) and strategy.position_size == 0
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, stop = math.round(close * 1.002, 2))
if strategy.position_size > 0 and bar_index - strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(0) >= 3
    strategy.close("L", comment="timeout")
